  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 209 AM EST Sat Nov 7 2026\n\nBy Monday afternoon and evening a low pressure system will have \npushed into the northeast with our area under a more zonal flow \nwith an area of low pressure over Mexico into the SW and Texas. \nThis pattern will generally be what we are under through Tuesday. \nBeginning on Tuesday the low pressure system begins to track east \ninto the Arklatex but at this time moisture looks on track to stay\nsouth of the area and stick to the Gulf. This will result in rain\nchances less than 10% through mid next week. Temperatures will \ndecrease into the 30s overnight beginning as early as Saturday \nmorning and lasting through at least Tuesday morning. This will \nlikely warrant frost/freeze products as the growing season \ncontinues in north Georgia. High temps will also lower into the \nmid to upper 60s this weekend. Rain chances may return late next \nweek into next weekend with broad troughing over much of the \neastern CONUS potentially bringing in moisture from the west as an\narea of low pressure pushes into the gulf. Looking to the long \nterm, the CPC has placed our area in a slight risk for below \nnormal temperatures. We are looking at the potential for a deep \ntrough over the southeast bringing in cooler air from Canada. This\nwill be yet another shot of cold air likely although it's a bit \ntoo soon to talk about how low the temps will get.",
